# How omdrop-owl runs AWDL on each Wi-Fi driver. One line per kernel driver,
# named as in /sys/class/net/<iface>/device/driver. A card whose driver isn't
# listed falls back to the "*" line, and only runs with /etc/omdrop/allow-untested.
# /etc/omdrop/owl-profiles, in the same format, is read before this file: try
# settings for your card there. To add your card here, see README.md, "Adding
# your card".
#
#   status     tested: works out of the box; untested: needs allow-untested
#   mode       shared: AWDL shares the AP's channel and Wi-Fi stays connected
#              exclusive: Wi-Fi is disconnected for the window, for cards that
#              can't inject, or hear AWDL, while associated (README)
#   mon_mac    station: the monitor interface carries the station's MAC, and OWL
#              reads it from there; own: it keeps a MAC of its own and OWL is
#              given the station's (owl -m)
#   reconnect  yes: force a reconnect after deleting the monitor interface, for
#              drivers whose station stops receiving after that
#   mt76_pm    yes: turn mt76 runtime power management off for the window
#   exclusive_backend
#              ibss: join AWDL's BSSID on awdlibss0 (or the station itself),
#              inject through a passive mon0
#              active-monitor: an active mon0 ACKs the phone's unicast itself;
#              the station becomes a passive monitor for the window, which is
#              what tunes the radio, and gets its type back on stop. Needs
#              hardware active-monitor support and mon_mac=station.
#              Ignored in shared mode. A line without this field is ibss.
#              (t4t5/omdrop-owl pull request 13, ported.)
#   notes      the rest of the line: the hardware, and what was observed
#
# driver   status    mode       mon_mac  reconnect  mt76_pm  exclusive_backend  notes
mt7925e    tested    shared     station  yes        yes      ibss               MediaTek MT7925 (Framework 13). Injects while associated, sending from the station's MAC; the station ACKs the phone's unicast. Without a reconnect, the station stops receiving 3-165 s after a monitor interface is deleted.
iwlwifi    tested    exclusive  station  no         no       ibss               Intel AX200 (kernel 6.19.8), AX201 (kernels 6.8 and 7.2.9), AX211 (kernels 7.0 and 7.2.3) and BE on Panther Lake (kernel 7.2). Associated, the firmware passes up no AWDL frames. Starts no ad-hoc cell on 5 GHz, so runs on channel 6: a 2.4 MB photo from an iPhone in 17 s, to it in 10.5 s. Some AX211s refuse an ad-hoc vif beside the station, so the station becomes the cell. The Wireless-AC 8260 (firmware 8000C-36) crashes on 5 GHz and never completed a transfer on 6.
mt76x2u    tested    exclusive  station  no         no       active-monitor     MediaTek MT7612U USB (0e8d:7612, Alfa AWUS036ACM), kernel 7.2.9 (pull request 13). Active mon0, the station as a passive monitor. Images both directions on channel 6; sending uses the BLE wake. Can transmit on 44 and 149 where the regulatory domain allows.
*          untested  shared     station  yes        no       ibss               Any other card. Needs monitor-mode injection while associated, and an AP on channel 6, 44 or 149.
